{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792951724,"nonce":"/3NvbsCJYviRR1bDSJ/RbQlfBNo=","title":"Match browser platform in command keys","message":"Welcome used the Mac Shift glyph even beside Ctrl on non-Mac visitors. Its keycap order was hardcoded independently of Chord.label. Also the bootstrap retained a RAYDE_VISITOR value in the query string, allowing a copied URL or bookmark to pin another platform. Derive the visitor afresh from browser platform information before startup, use the same platform-aware keycap formatter as shortcut labels, and verify the real Mac/Windows/Linux page and modifier bindings. Related browser run issue 87a3c309b1fc6f24e8380f66ff8250c43e67016db2a09dcf2022e021bf435ad0.","files":null}]}